{"id": "DfQ4HtpoHDO", "title": "Video by vigyan_bhairav__", "description": "Method 4: The Peaceful One 🕊️🌕🕉️\n\nAt the end of every breath, there is a moment of perfect silence. Most of us never notice it. The Vigyan Bhairav Tantra says something is shining there.\n\nThe breath flows out: rechaka.\nIt flows back in: puraka.\nAnd between them, it rests: kumbhaka.\n\nThere are two quiet pauses:\n🌌 The outer pause, bahya kumbhaka: after the breath goes out and rests in the space beyond.\n🫀 The inner pause, antar kumbhaka: when it returns and rests in the heart.\n\nIn these pauses, the living power of the breath, Shakti, has nothing left to do. So, on her own, she comes to rest.\n\nWhen the power rests, it melts into awareness itself. The two become one. What remains is pure light, with no name and no form.\n\nThe Tantra calls it Shanta, the Peaceful One. Your own true Self. ✨\n\nAs long as the breath keeps the power busy, this light stays hidden. When every thought falls silent, it reveals itself.\n\n⚠️ Never hold or force the breath. Just notice the natural pause at the end of each out-breath and each in-breath, and rest there.\n\n🧘 Try it: for the next 5 breaths, simply pause your attention at the end of each one. Comment 🕊️ if you felt the peace.\n\n📖 Vigyan Bhairav Tantra, Dharana 4 (verse 27)\n⬅️ New here? Start with Method 1 on my page.\nFollow for one method at a time 🪷\n\n#VigyanBhairavTantra #VigyanBhairav #Bhairava #Shiva #Shakti #Tantra #KashmirShaivism #Kumbhaka #Pranayama #Prana #Shanta #InnerPeace #TrueSelf #BreathAwareness #Meditation #Mindfulness #Stillness #Samadhi #SpiritualAwakening #Consciousness #Yoga #Mahadev #HarHarMahadev #Ukiyoe #WoodblockPrint #MeditationReels #SpiritualReels #ReelsIndia", "channel": "vigyan_bhairav__", "uploader_id": "70392958166", "uploader": "Bhairav", "timestamp": 1793675244, "like_count": 1352, "comment_count": 9, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gec